# Core Directives

- Act as an expert software engineer prioritizing maintainability and execution speed.
- Prefer clear, concise implementations over clever abstractions.
- Default to Hexagonal Architecture (Ports and Adapters).
- Optimize for performance only when readability remains high.
- Apply DRY and remove repeated logic.

## Done Checks

- Domain logic is isolated from frameworks and transport details.
- Names and function boundaries are intention-revealing.
- Changes include only necessary complexity.
